Has dladdr find a static program as the object an address of it is in,
as patch 0030 has dlsym find nothing in one: it looked through the
program's symbols by its hash table, which a static program has none
of, and stopped the program on an assertion ("unexpected hash style").
dladdr now gives the program's path and no symbol, as musl's does.
CPython's stack unwinding test asks it of its frames. Meant for
upstream.

